--shotcount-pervisoroutreachutorontobowangv1-alternative
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear Professor Wang,

I am preparing an application to the Cell and Systems Biology PhD at University of Toronto for Fall 2026, and I am writing to ask about potential PhD supervision.

Your GraphComm work on cell-cell communication using graph-based deep learning and spatial single-cell RNA sequencing is the clearest connection to my proposed direction. I was especially interested in how the method combines neighbourhood information with intracellular signalling rather than treating ligand-receptor pairs in isolation.

My confirmed research experience includes analysing single-cell RNA sequencing data with Python and building reproducible feature pipelines. I am now developing a proposal around interpretable graph models for spatial cell communication, grounded in the same methodological questions. My current role is research assistant at a synthetic computational biology lab.

Would you be considering new doctoral students for Fall 2026, and would this direction merit a short conversation about fit and supervision?

If this direction is within your current supervision plans, I would appreciate any guidance on whether you are considering new doctoral students and whether an initial conversation would be useful. I have attached my programme-specific CV for context.

Thank you for your time and for your work on graph models for cell communication.

Kind regards,
Amara Okafor
--shotcount-pervisoroutreachutorontobowangv1-alternative
Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

<p>Dear Professor Wang,</p>
<p>I am preparing an application to the Cell and Systems Biology PhD at University of Toronto for Fall 2026, and I am writing to ask about potential PhD supervision.</p>
<p>Your GraphComm work on cell-cell communication using graph-based deep learning and spatial single-cell RNA sequencing is the clearest connection to my proposed direction. I was especially interested in how the method combines neighbourhood information with intracellular signalling rather than treating ligand-receptor pairs in isolation.</p>
<p>My confirmed research experience includes analysing single-cell RNA sequencing data with Python and building reproducible feature pipelines. I am now developing a proposal around interpretable graph models for spatial cell communication, grounded in the same methodological questions. My current role is research assistant at a synthetic computational biology lab.</p>
<p>Would you be considering new doctoral students for Fall 2026, and would this direction merit a short conversation about fit and supervision?</p>
<p>If this direction is within your current supervision plans, I would appreciate any guidance on whether you are considering new doctoral students and whether an initial conversation would be useful. I have attached my programme-specific CV for context.</p>
<p>Thank you for your time and for your work on graph models for cell communication.</p>
<p>Kind regards,<br>Amara Okafor</p>
--shotcount-pervisoroutreachutorontobowangv1-alternative--
